instructions:
The scaffolded package is generic — all per-project identity (worker name, R2 bucket, GitHub connector target) lives in the instance files, not in wrangler.jsonc.

Create two instance files in packages/infra/environments/<env>/:

   // warehouse-bucket.ts — the R2 bucket for raw + marts
   import { r2Module } from '../../modules/r2'
   export default r2Module.instance({
     name: 'warehouse-bucket',
     config: { accountId: '<account id>', bucketName: '<project>-warehouse' },
   })

   // warehouse.ts — the worker + container
   import { cloudflareModule } from '../../modules/cloudflare'
   import warehouseBucket from './warehouse-bucket'
   export default cloudflareModule.instance({
     name: 'warehouse',
     imports: [warehouseBucket],
     config: {
       workdir: 'packages/warehouse',
       accountId: '<account id>',
       workerName: '<project>-warehouse',
       workerSecrets: ['WAREHOUSE_TOKEN', 'GITHUB_TOKEN'],
       workerVars: [
         { name: 'GITHUB_OWNER', value: '<github org/user>' },
         { name: 'GITHUB_REPO', value: '<github repo>' }
       ],
       r2Bindings: [{ binding: 'WAREHOUSE_BUCKET', from: 'warehouse-bucket', output: 'bucketName' }],
       immediateContainerRollout: true,
     },
   })

Add WAREHOUSE_TOKEN (any long random string, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32` — gates the mart-read API) and GITHUB_TOKEN (a fine-grained PAT with read-only repo access, scoped to the repo set in GITHUB_OWNER/GITHUB_REPO — used only inside the one-shot materialize run, never reachable from the mart-read API) to secrets.yaml. CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN needs Workers Scripts: Edit, Workers R2 Storage: Edit, and Containers: Edit.

`zbc apply <env>` provisions the bucket and deploys the worker + container (Docker must be running locally). The daily Cron Trigger (wrangler.jsonc's `triggers.crons`) runs the first materialize automatically; trigger one manually with `POST /materialize` (bearer WAREHOUSE_TOKEN) instead of waiting for the schedule. Read a mart with `GET /marts/<name>` (bearer WAREHOUSE_TOKEN) — 404 for both a missing and a malformed name, by design (no enumeration oracle).

To add a mart: add a dbt model under dbt/models/marts/ with an `external` materialization (writes parquet to the mart's declared R2 path) and its columns declared with `description` + `data_type` in the model's schema.yml entry — a model without a description fails the materialize run rather than shipping an undocumented mart. To add a connector beyond the shipped GitHub one, add a dlt source under connectors/ and wire it into container/materialize.ts's extract step.
